{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.1", "U6.2", "U7.1"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "U7.1"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the SS2040FL U6 is drawn with its anode (pin 1, triangle base) tied to the BAT+ label and its cathode (pin 2, bar side) tied to the battery positive terminal U7.1. The battery negative U7.2 goes to BAT-, so the diode sits with cathode toward the cell and anode toward the system rail.",
      "expected": "The specification states the battery feeds BAT+ through U6 with the anode on the battery side: 'Battery (U7, 18650 holder) → pin 1 → Net-(U6-A) → U6 (SS2040FL) anode→cathode → BAT+'. The diode-OR requires anode = battery+, cathode = BAT+.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Battery (U7, 18650 holder) → pin 1 → Net-(U6-A) → U6 (SS2040FL) anode→cathode → BAT+."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower.kicad_sch: U6 SS2040FL pin1 (anode) wired to BAT+ label, pin2 (cathode) wired to U7 + (MH1); U7 - (MH2) to BAT-."}
      ],
      "impact": "The 18650 cell is reverse-biased off the BAT+ rail, so the battery cannot power the board; conversely any USB/adapter voltage present on BAT+ forward-biases into the raw cell (back-feed), the exact opposite of the documented isolation function.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the input decoupling capacitor C1 across the boost input (Display_Power_Switch) node is valued 0.1 µF / 16 V.",
      "expected": "The specification's component-matching table lists schematic C1 among the 1 µF / 25 V group: 'C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: C1 = 0.1uF/16V between Display_Power_Switch node and GND."}
      ],
      "impact": "Reduced bulk capacitance and lower voltage rating on the EPD boost input than the reference design; may increase input ripple / reduce noise margin of the display power stage.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended design in at least one clear way: the battery-isolation Schottky U6 is installed with reversed polarity (anode on BAT+, cathode on the cell), which contradicts the spec's diode-OR description and would both disable battery power and allow adapter back-feed into the cell. A secondary, lower-confidence deviation is C1 being 0.1 µF/16 V where the spec's reference table specifies 1 µF/25 V."
}

